 "about": "Blend Buddies word list for final /ks/. S is the friendly letter and starts on the right, sliding left to join K. Words spelled with x (fox) represent /ks/ with the letter x in the written word; the buddies are still K and S. 'without' is the real word you get when the final /s/ is left out (empty = not a pair word). Only real, child-friendly words are used as pairs (not box/bock, and never a pair that would make a swear word). 'pre' is the spelling before k (or before x). 'mid' is a letter between k and s in the spelling (the silent e in rakes). 'spell' is x when /ks/ is written as x. Link a word with ?w=<word>. 'pairs' lists the word ids used on the listen slides (?mp=<id>). The list is also embedded in words.js so the page works when opened as a file.",
